## Linked Issues
**Issue #51 - "Unexpected == evaluation of unknown values with svunit_testcase::fail()"** (closed by this PR).

Issue body (verbatim from the source URL):
"Since the fail() method takes a two-state argument of type bit for the expression argument, the evaluation for unknown values is inconsistent with pure SystemVerilog code due to the implicit type casting.

The expression 1'bx == 1'bx evaluates to X and branches to the else clause in the following code.

    if(1'bx == 1'bx) $display(\"true\");
    else    $display(\"false\");

However, when the same expression is used in the `FAIL_UNLESS macro it will not generate an error.  A proposed fix is to change the b argument of the svunit_testcase::fail() function to a logic type and change the test operation from if(b) to if(b!==0)."
